#!/usr/bin/env ady2nim
#ady2nim-args js
"""
page_alone.ady -- a page that htmx draws, with no server: its requests answered in the page

An app of BROWSER_EXAMPLES answers each request from a session (DIJKSTRA_HTMX's
dijkstra_events_gui.ady), which knows nothing of HTTP: the server hands it every request, and tells
every open page of each change. The session compiles to JavaScript as well, and then the page can
be its own server: a script that makes the session, and hands it every request htmx and the
page's script make, in place of a server. The page's script and htmx do not know the difference.

    serve_in_page(answer, shell)    every request the page makes, from now on, is answered by
                                    ANSWER(method, path, fields), as a server's handler would
                                    (its fields the query and the body, "a=1&b=2"; "" when there
                                    is no such thing); then the page is SHELL, what the server
                                    answers to GET /
    tell_page(change)               CHANGE told to the page, as the server's GET /events tells
                                    it (page_board's changes_channel hears it)

The script is the page's first, alone in an index.html beside it, so that it is there before htmx
and the page's script ask anything:

    <!doctype html><script src="dijkstra_alone.js"></script>

and in it, what the server does:

    var session: Session = Session("graph.txt")         # kept in the browser (kept.ady)

    def answer(method: str, path: str, fields: str) -> str:
        return session.answer(method, path, fields)

    serve_in_page(answer, shell_text())

The page's other scripts are named in SHELL by a path from the page ("htmx.min.js"), so the
page opens from a file as well as from a site.
"""

